{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Retro",
  "theme": "retro",
  "_about": "Retro HUD, generated by design/gen_hud.py: an 80s digital readout in amber. A segmented rev bar across the top (green, amber from the shift zone, red at the redline), the gear in seven-segment digits (DSEG7 Classic, SIL OFL) on the left, boost, oil and water as seven-segment figures with bar graphs on the right. Fitted (Nov 9 2026) to the HUD as BMW's own height-adjust frame shows it, x 120..680, y 100..380, and kept clear of the bottom-left x 120..350, y 235..380, where BMW draws its speed and speed-limit sign (and in Sport its rev band) over ours. To change it, copy this file into the app data folder layouts/ (scripts/deploy.sh); the app reloads it by itself. Widget types and tokens: see the header of hud.js.",
